-- nolhivaram
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Nolhivaram Island?","answer":"Due to the island''s remote location in the northern atolls, direct public ferry services from Male are limited. Most guesthouses can arrange the complete transfer from Male, including the domestic flight and speedboat connection. When planning your journey, remember that weather conditions can occasionally affect flight schedules in this region, so it''s advisable to allow buffer days in your travel plans. The journey to Nolhivaram is part of the adventure, offering beautiful aerial views of the Maldivian atolls during the flight and a chance to experience the stunning blue waters during the speedboat transfer."},{"question":"What makes Nolhivaram''s lacquerware traditions unique in the Maldives?","answer":"Nolhivaram''s lacquerware traditions stand out in the Maldives because the island has preserved comprehensive knowledge of traditional lacquerwork (liyelaa jehun) that combines artistic expression with functional craftsmanship. The island is particularly known for its expertise in creating vibrant, multi-layered lacquer finishes that feature distinctive color combinations and intricate patterns, demonstrating exceptional control over this challenging medium. Nolhivaram artisans maintain deep knowledge of resin preparation, understanding how to extract, process, and apply natural tree resins that form the base of traditional lacquer. The community has preserved specialized techniques for creating and applying natural pigments, resulting in a distinctive palette that gives Nolhivaram lacquerware its recognizable character. What makes Nolhivaram special is the integration of geometric patterns with stylized natural motifs, creating designs that reflect both Islamic artistic traditions and elements unique to Maldivian culture. The island maintains knowledge of incising techniques that allow artisans to create detailed patterns by carefully carving through layers of colored lacquer to reveal contrasting colors beneath. Nolhivaram is also known for its finishing methods that produce an exceptionally high gloss and durable surface, protecting the decorated pieces while enhancing their visual appeal. These preserved traditions offer visitors insights into a sophisticated decorative art that connects to centuries of Maldivian cultural heritage while demonstrating remarkable adaptation to the materials available in the island environment."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Nolhivaram Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Nolhivaram Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. For those interested in experiencing the island''s lacquerware traditions, this dry season is also excellent as many artisanal activities take place outdoors, and the drier conditions are better for lacquer application and drying. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. This season can still be good for cultural experiences and indoor craft demonstrations, though some outdoor activities may be affected by rain. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year. Due to Nolhivaram''s northern location, it may experience slightly different weather patterns than southern atolls, with the possibility of brief rain showers even during the dry season. The shoulder months of November and April often offer a good balance of favorable weather and lower visitor numbers."},{"question":"What type of accommodation can I expect on Nolhivaram?","answer":"Accommodation on Nolhivaram is limited and simple, reflecting the island''s authentic character and minimal tourism development. The island offers a small number of family-run guesthouses that provide clean, comfortable rooms with basic amenities including air conditioning, private bathrooms with hot water, and Wi-Fi (though connectivity may be inconsistent). Most accommodations offer full-board packages that include three home-cooked Maldivian meals daily, featuring fresh seafood caught by local fishermen. Some artisan families also offer homestay experiences where guests stay in a room within a family home, providing deeper cultural immersion and the opportunity to observe traditional lacquerwork up close. A few properties are located near the beach, offering easy access to the island''s beautiful shores. Luxury amenities are limited, and the focus is on authentic experiences rather than high-end facilities. What these accommodations lack in luxury, they make up for in personal service, cultural insights, and genuine hospitality. Visitors should adjust their expectations accordingly and embrace the opportunity to experience authentic island life rather than expecting resort-style amenities."},{"question":"Can I participate in lacquerwork activities as a visitor to Nolhivaram?","answer":"Yes, visitors to Nolhivaram have excellent opportunities to participate in lacquerwork activities, which is one of the island''s unique attractions. Most guesthouses can arrange for guests to visit traditional artisan workshops where you can observe master craftspeople at work and learn about the techniques and traditions of lacquerware creation. For those interested in hands-on experiences, basic lacquerwork workshops allow you to try simple decorative techniques and create small items under the guidance of skilled artisans. Material preparation demonstrations show how resins and pigments are processed and prepared for application. Pattern design sessions provide insights into the traditional motifs and their cultural significance, with opportunities to create your own designs based on traditional elements. For those with a deeper interest, extended workshops can sometimes be arranged where you can learn more advanced techniques or work on larger projects over several days. Some accommodations offer more immersive experiences where visitors can stay with artisan families, providing opportunities to observe and participate in the daily rhythm of this traditional craft. These activities provide not just entertainment but educational insights into a decorative art that has been part of Maldivian material culture for centuries. The level of participation can be adjusted based on your interest and time available, from brief introductory sessions to more in-depth learning experiences."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'nolhivaram';


-- nolhivaranfaru
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Nolhivaranfaru Island?","answer":"Due to the island''s remote location in the northern atolls, direct public ferry services from Male are limited. Most guesthouses can arrange the complete transfer from Male, including the domestic flight and speedboat connection. When planning your journey, remember that weather conditions can occasionally affect flight schedules in this region, so it''s advisable to allow buffer days in your travel plans. The journey to Nolhivaranfaru is part of the adventure, offering beautiful aerial views of the Maldivian atolls during the flight and a chance to experience the stunning blue waters during the speedboat transfer."},{"question":"What makes Nolhivaranfaru''s textile traditions unique in the Maldives?","answer":"Nolhivaranfaru''s textile traditions stand out in the Maldives because the island has preserved comprehensive knowledge of traditional weaving that combines artistic expression with practical functionality. The island is particularly known for its expertise in handloom weaving, where artisans create distinctive patterns and textures using techniques that have been refined over generations. Nolhivaranfaru weavers maintain deep knowledge of fiber preparation, understanding how to process and prepare natural materials like cotton and coconut fiber for different textile applications. The community has preserved specialized techniques for creating intricate patterns through the manipulation of warp and weft threads, resulting in textiles with distinctive visual and tactile qualities. What makes Nolhivaranfaru special is the integration of geometric patterns with stylized natural motifs, creating designs that reflect both Islamic artistic traditions and elements unique to Maldivian culture. The island maintains knowledge of natural dyeing methods, using plants, minerals, and other natural materials to create a palette of colors that gives Nolhivaranfaru textiles their recognizable character. Nolhivaranfaru is also known for its finishing techniques that enhance the durability and appearance of woven items, ensuring they can withstand daily use while maintaining their beauty. These preserved traditions offer visitors insights into a sophisticated textile art that connects to centuries of Maldivian cultural heritage while demonstrating remarkable adaptation to the materials available in the island environment."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Nolhivaranfaru Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Nolhivaranfaru Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. For those interested in experiencing the island''s textile traditions, this dry season is also excellent as many weaving activities take place outdoors, and the drier conditions are better for fiber preparation and dyeing. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. This season can still be good for cultural experiences and indoor weaving demonstrations, though some outdoor activities may be affected by rain. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year. Due to Nolhivaranfaru''s northern location, it may experience slightly different weather patterns than southern atolls, with the possibility of brief rain showers even during the dry season. The shoulder months of November and April often offer a good balance of favorable weather and lower visitor numbers."},{"question":"What type of accommodation can I expect on Nolhivaranfaru?","answer":"Accommodation on Nolhivaranfaru is limited and simple, reflecting the island''s authentic character and minimal tourism development. The island offers a small number of family-run guesthouses that provide clean, comfortable rooms with basic amenities including air conditioning, private bathrooms with hot water, and Wi-Fi (though connectivity may be inconsistent). Most accommodations offer full-board packages that include three home-cooked Maldivian meals daily, featuring fresh seafood caught by local fishermen. Some weaving families also offer homestay experiences where guests stay in a room within a family home, providing deeper cultural immersion and the opportunity to observe traditional textile arts up close. A few properties are located near the beach, offering easy access to the island''s beautiful shores. Luxury amenities are limited, and the focus is on authentic experiences rather than high-end facilities. What these accommodations lack in luxury, they make up for in personal service, cultural insights, and genuine hospitality. Visitors should adjust their expectations accordingly and embrace the opportunity to experience authentic island life rather than expecting resort-style amenities."},{"question":"Can I participate in weaving activities as a visitor to Nolhivaranfaru?","answer":"Yes, visitors to Nolhivaranfaru have excellent opportunities to participate in weaving activities, which is one of the island''s unique attractions. Most guesthouses can arrange for guests to visit traditional weaving workshops where you can observe master artisans at work and learn about the techniques and traditions of textile creation. For those interested in hands-on experiences, basic weaving workshops allow you to try simple techniques and create small textile items under the guidance of skilled weavers. Fiber preparation demonstrations show how natural materials are processed and prepared for weaving. Pattern design sessions provide insights into the traditional motifs and their cultural significance, with opportunities to create your own designs based on traditional elements. For those with a deeper interest, extended workshops can sometimes be arranged where you can learn more advanced techniques or work on larger projects over several days. Some accommodations offer more immersive experiences where visitors can stay with weaving families, providing opportunities to observe and participate in the daily rhythm of this traditional craft. These activities provide not just entertainment but educational insights into a textile art that has been part of Maldivian material culture for centuries. The level of participation can be adjusted based on your interest and time available, from brief introductory sessions to more in-depth learning experiences."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'nolhivaranfaru';


-- noomaraa
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Shaviyani Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,200 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.4 km long, 0.8 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"198 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Pristine culture, serene beaches, excellent tranquility"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, tranquility seekers, nature lovers"}],"island_overview":["Bileffahi Island is a pristine local island in Shaviyani Atoll that offers visitors a serene glimpse into traditional Maldivian life in the northern region of the archipelago. This tranquil island combines natural beauty with a peaceful atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking calm cultural experiences and serene tropical surroundings.","Known for its serene beaches, pristine coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Bileffahi provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s tranquil community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their peaceful way of life with pristine hospitality.","What makes Bileffahi special is its pristine natural environment and serene northern location. Visitors can enjoy tranquil beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience peaceful island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the pristine Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Bileffahi Island is pristinely located in the northern part of Shaviyani Atoll, approximately 198 kilometers from Male. This location provides a pristine and serene experience in the northern Maldives, while maintaining good accessibility through seaplane transfers or domestic flights.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to serene coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Shaviyani Atoll in its most pristine form."]},{"heading":"Bileffahi: Pristine Paradise & Marine Serenity","paragraphs":["Bileffahi Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring serene white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most pristine marine environments in Shaviyani Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a tranquil, peaceful setting."]},{"heading":"Serene White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Bileffahi features pristine white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and tranquil beach activities."]},{"heading":"Pristine House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers serene snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Tranquil Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the peaceful spirit of traditional northern island life with friendly locals and pristine Maldivian culture in a tranquil community setting."]},{"heading":"Peaceful Cultural Heritage","paragraphs":["Discover the island''s rich cultural traditions and learn about traditional practices that make this community pristine in the northern Maldives."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Bileffahi''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Bileffahi feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Bileffahi offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and pristine activities. The island''s tranquil environment and peaceful atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a serene, calming setting."]},{"heading":"Pristine House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the tranquil house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in pristine waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby serene dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in pristine marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, serene sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Shaviyani Atoll with tranquil exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in pristine community settings."]},{"heading":"Peaceful Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience pristine Maldivian island life with tranquil cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy serene sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in pristine waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Bileffahi is home to approximately 1,200 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and pristine cultural traditions that create a tranquil atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Bileffahi follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains a pristine atmosphere where visitors can experience tranquil Maldivian culture and customs in their most peaceful, serene setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this pristine island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Bileffahi has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and pristine cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Bileffahi Island?","answer":"Regular inter-island ferry services are also available between Shaviyani Atoll islands."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Bileffahi?","answer":"The best time to visit Bileffahi is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more pristine local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Bileffahi?","answer":"Bileffahi offers various accommodations including pristine guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a tranquil setting."},{"question":"What makes Bileffahi''s pristine nature special?","answer":"Bileffahi is known for its pristine and tranquil natural environment in the northern Maldives. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a peaceful atmosphere perfect for serene exploration. Visitors can experience calming cultural exchanges and participate in pristine community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["foakaidhoo","feydhoo","feevah","bileffahi","narudhoo","milandhoo","maroshi","maaungoodhoo","lhaimagu","komandoo","kanditheemu","goidhoo","funadhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'noomaraa';


-- olhuvelifushi
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Lhaviyani Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 600 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"0.7 km long, 0.3 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"130 km"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Pristine beaches, excellent snorkeling, peaceful vibe"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Nature lovers, snorkelers, cultural travelers"}],"island_overview":["Located in the breathtaking Lhaviyani Atoll, Olhuvelifushi Island offers visitors an authentic Maldivian experience away from the crowds. This picturesque island combines natural beauty with traditional island life.","Olhuvelifushi is known for its long stretches of pristine beaches, excellent snorkeling spots, and peaceful atmosphere. The island maintains its traditional charm while welcoming visitors with genuine hospitality.","What makes Olhuvelifushi special is its unspoiled environment, rich marine biodiversity, and the opportunity to experience local culture in a relaxed setting."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Olhuvelifushi Island is situated in the northern part of Lhaviyani Atoll, approximately 130 kilometers from Male. This location offers easy access to some of the best dive sites in the Maldives while maintaining a tranquil island atmosphere.","The island''s position provides natural protection from strong currents while offering access to vibrant coral reefs and abundant marine life."]},{"heading":"Olhuvelifushi: Natural Beauty & Marine Life","paragraphs":["Olhuvelifushi Island boasts stunning natural beauty with powder-soft white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and healthy coral reefs teeming with marine life."]},{"heading":"Pristine White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Olhuvelifushi features some of the most beautiful beaches in Lhaviyani Atoll, perfect for relaxation and beach walks."]},{"heading":"Excellent Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef offers easy access to colorful coral formations and diverse marine life."]},{"heading":"Authentic Island Culture","paragraphs":["Experience genuine Maldivian hospitality and traditional island life."]},{"heading":"Sandbank Visits","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks for the ultimate tropical island experience."]},{"heading":"Beach Highlights","paragraphs":["Olhuvelifushi''s coastal features include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The island''s underwater world features:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Olhuvelifushi offers a variety of activities focused on marine adventures, cultural experiences, and relaxation."]},{"heading":"Snorkeling Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore vibrant coral reefs teeming with tropical fish."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving","paragraphs":["Discover world-class dive sites in Lhaviyani Atoll."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands to experience different aspects of the Maldives."]},{"heading":"Fishing Excursions","paragraphs":["Join local fishermen for traditional fishing experiences."]},{"heading":"Cultural Experiences","paragraphs":["Learn about traditional Maldivian crafts and daily life."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy breathtaking sunsets over the Indian Ocean."]},{"heading":"People & Community Life","paragraphs":["Olhuvelifushi is home to a close-knit community of approximately 600 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism."]},{"heading":"Daily Life","paragraphs":["Life on Olhuvelifushi revolves around fishing, tourism, and community activities. The island has a peaceful rhythm that reflects traditional Maldivian values."]},{"heading":"Culture & Traditions","paragraphs":["Olhuvelifushi preserves authentic Maldivian cultural traditions including music, dance, and handicrafts. The community celebrates Islamic festivals with enthusiasm."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Olhuvelifushi Island?","answer":"There''s also a public ferry option that takes 6-7 hours."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Olhuvelifushi?","answer":"The best time is during the dry season from December to April, but Olhuvelifushi can be visited year-round."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["hinnavaru","kurendhoo","naifaru"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'olhuvelifushi';


-- omadhoo-thaa
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Thaa Atoll, Central Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,400 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.5 km long, 0.8 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"198 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Spectacular culture, pristine beaches, excellent snorkeling"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, snorkelers, authentic experiences"}],"island_overview":["Omadhoo Island is a spectacular local island in Thaa Atoll that offers visitors an authentic glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. This outstanding island combines natural beauty with a genuine atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking exceptional cultural experiences and pristine tropical surroundings.","Known for its beautiful beaches, spectacular coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Omadhoo provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s authentic community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their outstanding way of life with spectacular hospitality.","What makes Omadhoo special is its spectacular natural environment and authentic island setting. Visitors can enjoy pristine beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience genuine island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the spectacular Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Omadhoo Island is beautifully located in the central part of Thaa Atoll, approximately 198 kilometers from Male. This location provides a spectacular and authentic experience while maintaining good accessibility to the capital and international airport through various transfer options.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to pristine coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Thaa Atoll in its most spectacular form."]},{"heading":"Omadhoo: Spectacular Paradise & Marine Authenticity","paragraphs":["Omadhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring pristine white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most spectacular marine environments in Thaa Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in an authentic, genuine setting."]},{"heading":"Pristine White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Omadhoo features spectacular white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and authentic beach activities."]},{"heading":"Spectacular House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers outstanding snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Authentic Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the genuine spirit of traditional island life with friendly locals and spectacular Maldivian culture in an authentic community setting."]},{"heading":"Outstanding Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks and spectacular islands around Omadhoo for pristine tropical paradise experiences with rich marine life."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Omadhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Omadhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Omadhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and spectacular activities. The island''s authentic environment and genuine atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a pristine, outstanding setting."]},{"heading":"Spectacular House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the authentic house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in spectacular waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby pristine dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in spectacular marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, pristine sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Thaa Atoll with authentic exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in spectacular community settings."]},{"heading":"Authentic Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience spectacular Maldivian island life with genuine cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy pristine sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in spectacular waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Omadhoo is home to approximately 1,400 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and spectacular cultural traditions that create an authentic atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Omadhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains a spectacular atmosphere where visitors can experience authentic Maldivian culture and customs in their most genuine, outstanding setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this spectacular island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Omadhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and spectacular cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Omadhoo Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Thaa Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Omadhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Omadhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more spectacular local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Omadhoo?","answer":"Omadhoo offers various accommodations including spectacular guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in an authentic setting."},{"question":"What makes Omadhoo''s authenticity special?","answer":"Omadhoo is known for its spectacular and authentic natural environment. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a genuine atmosphere perfect for outstanding exploration. Visitors can experience exceptional cultural exchanges and participate in spectacular community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["guraidhoo","gaadhiffushi","dhiyamigili","burunee","vilufushi","veymandoo","vandhoo","thimarafushi","omadhoo","madifushi","kinbidhoo","kandoodhoo","hirilandhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'omadhoo-thaa';


-- omadhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Omadhoo Island?","answer":"Omadhoo Island is accessible via several transportation options. The most common route is by public ferry from Male, which operates three times a week (Sunday, Tuesday, and Thursday), departing at 9:00 AM and arriving at Omadhoo around 2:00 PM. For a faster route, you can take a domestic flight from Velana International Airport to Maamigili (about 20 minutes), followed by a speedboat to Omadhoo (approximately 30 minutes). Most guesthouses can assist with arranging transfers and will provide detailed information about the best options based on your arrival date and preferences."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Omadhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Omadhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (November to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. January to March typically offers the most reliable weather conditions with minimal rainfall and gentle breezes. The southwest monsoon season (May to October) brings occasional rain showers and slightly rougher seas, though there are still many sunny days. This period offers advantages including fewer tourists, lower prices, and lush island vegetation. If you''re interested in whale shark encounters in the nearby South Ari Marine Protected Area, these gentle giants can be spotted year-round, though sightings may be more consistent from January to April. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year, making Omadhoo a viable destination in any season depending on your preferences."},{"question":"What makes Omadhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Omadhoo distinguishes itself from other local islands through its authentic preservation of traditional Maldivian life and relatively untouched natural environment. Unlike more developed islands that have seen significant tourism infrastructure, Omadhoo maintains its genuine character with a community still primarily engaged in traditional fishing and island activities. The island''s smaller size and population create an intimate atmosphere where visitors quickly feel welcomed as part of the community rather than just tourists. Omadhoo''s house reef is particularly impressive, with healthy coral formations accessible directly from shore, offering exceptional snorkeling without boat trips. The island''s central location in Alifu Dhaalu Atoll provides convenient access to whale shark areas, manta points, and other islands while remaining peaceful and uncrowded. Omadhoo also stands out for its strong fishing heritage, with visitors able to observe and participate in traditional fishing practices that have sustained the community for generations. For travelers seeking the increasingly rare experience of authentic Maldivian island life without sacrificing natural beauty or basic comforts, Omadhoo offers a perfect balance that''s becoming harder to find as tourism expands throughout the archipelago."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Omadhoo Island?","answer":"Yes, as Omadhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas. Both men and women should cover shoulders and knees when walking around the village, visiting shops, or dining in local establishments. Men should wear t-shirts/shirts and shorts that reach the knee or longer. Women should wear t-shirts/blouses with sleeves and skirts/shorts/pants that cover the knees. Lightweight, loose-fitting clothing is ideal given the tropical climate. Swimwear (including bikinis) is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach\" area on the northern shore of the island. When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads with a scarf. These dress code requirements are a sign of respect for local culture and traditions. It''s worth noting that on excursions to uninhabited islands, sandbanks, or during resort day trips, Western-style swimwear is generally acceptable. When packing for your trip, include modest clothing for island activities along with your regular beachwear for designated areas."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Omadhoo?","answer":"The waters around Omadhoo offer exceptional marine biodiversity, making it a paradise for snorkelers. The island''s house reef features healthy coral formations with both hard corals (brain coral, staghorn coral, table coral) and colorful soft corals creating a vibrant underwater landscape. Reef fish are abundant, including various species of butterflyfish, angelfish, parrotfish, surgeonfish, and triggerfish displaying spectacular colors. Blacktip and whitetip reef sharks are commonly spotted patrolling the reef edges, particularly in the morning and late afternoon. Green and hawksbill sea turtles can be observed feeding on seagrass beds or resting among coral formations. Various ray species inhabit the surrounding waters, including eagle rays and stingrays often seen gliding over sandy areas adjacent to the reef. Moray eels, octopus, and reef cuttlefish provide fascinating encounters for observant snorkelers exploring coral crevices. During certain seasons, schools of jackfish, tuna, and trevally create impressive underwater spectacles. The nearby channels occasionally attract larger pelagic species, while the South Ari Marine Protected Area offers the possibility of whale shark encounters on dedicated excursions."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'omadhoo';


-- raimmandhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Meemu Atoll, Central Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 550 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"0.7 km long, 0.3 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"140 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Pristine beaches, excellent snorkeling, peaceful atmosphere"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Nature lovers, snorkelers, cultural travelers, budget travelers"}],"island_overview":["Nestled in the heart of Meemu Atoll, Raimmandhoo Island offers visitors an authentic Maldivian experience away from the crowds. This peaceful local island combines natural beauty with rich cultural heritage.","Raimmandhoo is particularly known for its excellent snorkeling spots, pristine beaches, and friendly local community. The island maintains a relaxed pace of life while offering visitors comfortable accommodations and memorable experiences.","What makes Raimmandhoo special is its combination of natural beauty, authentic culture, and accessibility. Visitors can enjoy both relaxation and adventure while experiencing genuine Maldivian hospitality."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Raimmandhoo Island is situated in the central part of Meemu Atoll, approximately 140 kilometers south of Male. This location offers a perfect balance between accessibility and seclusion.","The island''s position in the atoll provides excellent access to some of the best snorkeling and diving sites in the region, while also offering protected lagoons perfect for swimming."]},{"heading":"Raimmandhoo: Natural Beauty & Marine Life","paragraphs":["Raimmandhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring powder-soft sand beaches, crystal-clear waters, and thriving marine ecosystems. The island offers a perfect tropical getaway for nature lovers."]},{"heading":"Pristine Beaches","paragraphs":["Raimmandhoo boasts stunning white sand beaches with gentle slopes into the lagoon, perfect for swimming and sunbathing."]},{"heading":"Vibrant Marine Life","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef teems with colorful fish and coral formations, offering excellent snorkeling opportunities."]},{"heading":"Authentic Culture","paragraphs":["Experience genuine Maldivian hospitality and traditional island life in a peaceful setting."]},{"heading":"Sandbank Excursions","paragraphs":["Visit nearby uninhabited sandbanks for the ultimate desert island experience with picnics and swimming."]},{"heading":"Beach Highlights","paragraphs":["Raimmandhoo''s coastal features include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The island''s underwater world features:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Raimmandhoo offers a variety of activities that showcase the island''s natural beauty and cultural heritage. From water sports to cultural immersion, there''s something for every type of traveler."]},{"heading":"Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef just offshore, teeming with colorful fish and coral formations."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving","paragraphs":["Discover world-class dive sites around Meemu Atoll with professional guides."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands and sandbanks to experience different aspects of Meemu Atoll."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Join local fishermen for authentic fishing experiences using traditional techniques."]},{"heading":"Cultural Tours","paragraphs":["Learn about traditional Maldivian crafts, cuisine, and way of life from local residents."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy breathtaking sunsets aboard traditional dhonis, often with dolphin sightings."]},{"heading":"People & Community Life","paragraphs":["Raimmandhoo is home to a close-knit community of about 550 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian lifestyles while welcoming visitors with genuine hospitality."]},{"heading":"Daily Life","paragraphs":["Life on Raimmandhoo follows the rhythms of fishing and island living. Mornings begin with fishing trips, followed by community activities and family time in the evenings."]},{"heading":"Culture & Traditions","paragraphs":["The island preserves authentic Maldivian traditions including crafts like rope-making and boat-building, traditional music, and Islamic festivals celebrated with community feasts."]},{"heading":"Local Economy","paragraphs":["Fishing remains the primary occupation, supplemented by a growing tourism sector. Many families combine traditional livelihoods with guesthouse operations and tour services."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Raimmandhoo Island?","answer":"Raimmandhoo is accessible by domestic flight to Kadhdhoo Airport (45 minutes from Male) followed by a 40-minute speedboat ride. Seaplane transfers are also available but weather-dependent. There''s a weekly public ferry from Male taking 12-14 hours."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Raimmandhoo?","answer":"The dry season from December to April offers the most reliable weather, but Raimmandhoo can be visited year-round. The wet season (May-November) sees fewer visitors and lower rates."},{"question":"What types of accommodation are available?","answer":"All provide AC, private bathrooms, and authentic hospitality."},{"question":"What activities are available on Raimmandhoo?","answer":"Popular activities include snorkeling, diving, island hopping, fishing trips, cultural tours, and sunset cruises. The island is particularly known for its excellent snorkeling opportunities and authentic cultural experiences."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["kolhufushi","muli","maduvvaree","dhiggaru","naalaafushi","veyvah"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'raimmandhoo';


-- rakeedhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Vaavu Atoll, Central Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,200 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.1 km long, 0.6 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"75 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Speedboat or seaplane"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Remarkable culture, stunning beaches, excellent handicrafts"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, handicraft lovers, authentic experiences"}],"island_overview":["Rakeedhoo Island is a remarkable local island in Vaavu Atoll that offers visitors an authentic glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. This outstanding island combines natural beauty with a genuine atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking exceptional cultural experiences and stunning tropical surroundings.","Known for its beautiful beaches, remarkable coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Rakeedhoo provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s authentic community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their outstanding way of life with remarkable hospitality.","What makes Rakeedhoo special is its remarkable natural environment and authentic island setting. Visitors can enjoy stunning beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience genuine island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the remarkable Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Rakeedhoo Island is beautifully located in the heart of Vaavu Atoll, approximately 75 kilometers from Male. This location provides a remarkable and authentic experience while maintaining excellent accessibility to the capital and international airport through various transfer options.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to stunning coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Vaavu Atoll in its most remarkable form."]},{"heading":"Rakeedhoo: Remarkable Paradise & Marine Authenticity","paragraphs":["Rakeedhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring stunning white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most remarkable marine environments in Vaavu Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in an authentic, genuine setting."]},{"heading":"Stunning White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Rakeedhoo features remarkable white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and authentic beach activities."]},{"heading":"Remarkable House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers outstanding snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Authentic Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the genuine spirit of traditional island life with friendly locals and remarkable Maldivian culture in an authentic community setting."]},{"heading":"Outstanding Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks and remarkable islands around Rakeedhoo for stunning tropical paradise experiences with rich marine life."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Rakeedhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Rakeedhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Rakeedhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and remarkable activities. The island''s authentic environment and genuine atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a stunning, outstanding setting."]},{"heading":"Remarkable House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the authentic house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in remarkable waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby stunning dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in remarkable marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, stunning sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Vaavu Atoll with authentic exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in remarkable community settings."]},{"heading":"Authentic Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience remarkable Maldivian island life with genuine cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy stunning sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in remarkable waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Rakeedhoo is home to approximately 1,200 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and remarkable cultural traditions that create an authentic atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Rakeedhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains a remarkable atmosphere where visitors can experience authentic Maldivian culture and customs in their most genuine, outstanding setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this remarkable island environment."]},{"heading":"Handicraft Heritage","paragraphs":["Rakeedhoo is particularly renowned for its traditional handicrafts, including mat weaving, rope making, and coconut shell crafts. Visitors can learn these ancient skills from local artisans and purchase authentic handmade souvenirs."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Rakeedhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and remarkable cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Rakeedhoo Island?","answer":"Rakeedhoo Island can be reached by speedboat from Male (2 hours 5 minutes) or by seaplane (30 minutes, weather dependent). Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Vaavu Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Rakeedhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Rakeedhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more remarkable local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Rakeedhoo?","answer":"Rakeedhoo offers various accommodations including remarkable guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in an authentic setting."},{"question":"What makes Rakeedhoo''s handicrafts special?","answer":"Rakeedhoo is renowned for its traditional handicrafts including mat weaving, rope making, and coconut shell crafts. The island maintains ancient artisan skills passed down through generations, offering visitors authentic handmade souvenirs and cultural learning experiences."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["keyodhoo","thinadhoo","fulidhoo","felidhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'rakeedhoo';


-- rasdhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Rasdhoo Island from Male?","answer":"You can reach Rasdhoo Island from Male by public ferry or speedboat. The public ferry operates three times a week (Monday, Wednesday, and Saturday), departing from Male at 9:00 AM and arriving at Rasdhoo around 12:30 PM. Some guesthouses also offer private transfers for a higher fee. For early morning hammerhead shark dives, it''s recommended to arrive the day before."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Rasdhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Rasdhoo Island depends on your priorities. January to March offers the highest chance of hammerhead sightings. The northeast monsoon (December-April) generally provides the best overall weather conditions with less rainfall and lower humidity. The southwest monsoon (May-November) may have occasional rain showers but still offers many sunny days, fewer tourists, and better chances to see manta rays due to higher plankton levels. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) year-round."},{"question":"Do I need to be a certified diver to dive in Rasdhoo?","answer":"While many of Rasdhoo''s famous dive sites like Hammerhead Point require advanced certification due to depth and currents, there are options for divers of all levels. Beginners can take a Discover Scuba Diving course to experience diving under close supervision in shallow, calm waters. The house reef and some nearby sites are suitable for novice divers. For those wanting to get certified, all dive centers on Rasdhoo offer PADI and/or SSI certification courses from Open Water to advanced levels. Non-divers can still enjoy Rasdhoo''s marine life through snorkeling trips to the house reef and nearby coral gardens."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Rasdhoo Island?","answer":"Yes, as Rasdhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas. Both men and women should cover shoulders and knees when walking around the village, visiting shops, or dining in local restaurants. Swimwear (including bikinis) is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach\" area on the eastern side of the island. When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads with a scarf. These dress code requirements are a sign of respect for local culture and traditions and are generally well-enforced on the island."},{"question":"What facilities are available for non-divers on Rasdhoo?","answer":"While Rasdhoo is famous for diving, non-divers will find plenty to enjoy. The island offers excellent snorkeling directly from the beach, with equipment available for rent from guesthouses and dive centers. Water sports like kayaking, stand-up paddleboarding, and jet skiing are available. Cultural experiences include village tours, cooking classes, and traditional Boduberu performances. Excursions to nearby uninhabited islands, sandbanks, and resort day trips are popular. The bikini beach is perfect for swimming and sunbathing. Rasdhoo also has several cafes, restaurants, and shops to explore, plus opportunities to interact with the friendly local community."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'rasdhoo';


