-- rathafandhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Rathafandhoo Island?","answer":"Public ferry service operates weekly from Male (approximately 18-20 hours journey time). Private speedboat transfers can be arranged through guesthouses (approximately 7 hours from Male)."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Rathafandhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Rathafandhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. For whale shark encounters, visit during the southwest monsoon (May to December). Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year."},{"question":"What makes Rathafandhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Rathafandhoo stands out for its exceptional preservation of traditional Maldivian life in a remote setting and its agricultural traditions. Unlike more developed islands, Rathafandhoo maintains its authentic character with a community still primarily engaged in traditional fishing and small-scale farming. The island offers access to Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll''s spectacular marine life while providing a genuine cultural experience away from mass tourism."},{"question":"Can I sample local produce on Rathafandhoo Island?","answer":"Yes, Rathafandhoo offers excellent opportunities to sample fresh local produce. Most guesthouses serve meals featuring island-grown fruits and vegetables, and some offer farm tours where visitors can taste tropical fruits directly from the trees. The island''s agricultural traditions mean that seasonal fruits like papaya, banana, breadfruit, and coconut are readily available and often incorporated into traditional Maldivian dishes."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Rathafandhoo?","answer":"Rathafandhoo''s waters offer excellent marine biodiversity, including healthy coral formations with both hard and soft corals. Common sightings include reef sharks (particularly blacktip and whitetip), sea turtles, various ray species, and abundant reef fish. Seasonal visitors include whale sharks (May-December) and manta rays. The house reef provides easy access to this underwater world directly from shore."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'rathafandhoo';


-- thakandhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Thakandhoo Island?","answer":"Due to the island''s remote location in the northern atolls, direct public ferry services from Male are limited. Most guesthouses can arrange the complete transfer from Male, including the domestic flight and speedboat connection. When planning your journey, remember that weather conditions can occasionally affect flight schedules in this region, so it''s advisable to allow buffer days in your travel plans. The journey to Thakandhoo is part of the adventure, offering beautiful aerial views of the Maldivian atolls during the flight and a chance to experience the stunning blue waters during the speedboat transfer."},{"question":"What makes Thakandhoo''s agricultural traditions unique in the Maldives?","answer":"Thakandhoo''s agricultural traditions stand out in the Maldives because most Maldivian islands rely primarily on fishing rather than farming. The island has developed a strong agricultural heritage thanks to its relatively large size, fertile soil, and freshwater resources. Thakandhoo farmers have adapted traditional farming techniques to work within the constraints of a coral island environment, creating productive agricultural systems despite limited land area and challenging soil conditions. The island grows a diverse range of crops including tropical fruits like papaya, watermelon, and bananas, as well as vegetables such as pumpkin, eggplant, and leafy greens. Traditional knowledge of soil enrichment using natural materials like coconut husks and fish waste has been preserved and passed down through generations. The community has developed specialized irrigation methods to maximize the use of limited freshwater resources, including rainwater harvesting systems. Seasonal planting patterns have been established based on the monsoon cycles, demonstrating deep ecological knowledge. What makes Thakandhoo special is the integration of agriculture with fishing activities, creating a more diversified and resilient food system than most Maldivian islands. These preserved agricultural traditions offer visitors insights into sustainable island living practices and the opportunity to experience a different aspect of Maldivian culture beyond the typical fishing and tourism focus found on other islands."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Thakandhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Thakandhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. For those interested in experiencing the island''s agricultural traditions, this dry season also coincides with the harvest period for many fruits and vegetables, making it an excellent time to participate in farm tours and tastings. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. This season can be interesting for agricultural tourism as it''s when many crops are planted and fields are at their greenest, though some outdoor activities may be affected by rain. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year. Due to Thakandhoo''s northern location, it may experience slightly different weather patterns than southern atolls, with the possibility of brief rain showers even during the dry season. The shoulder months of November and April often offer a good balance of favorable weather and lower visitor numbers."},{"question":"What type of accommodation can I expect on Thakandhoo?","answer":"Accommodation on Thakandhoo is limited and simple, reflecting the island''s authentic character and minimal tourism development. The island offers a small number of family-run guesthouses that provide clean, comfortable rooms with basic amenities including air conditioning, private bathrooms with hot water, and Wi-Fi (though connectivity may be inconsistent). Most accommodations offer full-board packages that include three home-cooked Maldivian meals daily, featuring fresh produce from local farms and seafood caught by local fishermen. Some farming families also offer homestay experiences where guests stay in a room within a family home, providing deeper cultural immersion and the opportunity to participate in agricultural activities. A few properties are located near the beach, offering easy access to the island''s beautiful shores. Luxury amenities are limited, and the focus is on authentic experiences rather than high-end facilities. What these accommodations lack in luxury, they make up for in personal service, cultural insights, and genuine hospitality. Visitors should adjust their expectations accordingly and embrace the opportunity to experience authentic island life rather than expecting resort-style amenities."},{"question":"Can I participate in farming activities as a visitor to Thakandhoo?","answer":"Yes, visitors to Thakandhoo have excellent opportunities to participate in farming activities, which is one of the island''s unique attractions. Most guesthouses can arrange for guests to join local farmers in various agricultural activities, from planting and harvesting to food preparation using farm-fresh ingredients. Farm tours provide insights into the island''s agricultural practices, with opportunities to learn about tropical crop cultivation, irrigation techniques, and traditional farming knowledge. Fruit and vegetable harvesting experiences allow visitors to pick fresh produce directly from the fields and gardens, learning about different varieties and their uses in local cuisine. Cooking classes using farm-fresh ingredients provide a farm-to-table experience where you can learn to prepare traditional Maldivian dishes with produce you''ve helped harvest. Some accommodations offer more immersive experiences where visitors can participate in daily farming routines, from early morning watering to afternoon harvesting. These activities provide not just entertainment but educational insights into sustainable farming practices and food production. The level of participation can be adjusted based on your interest and experience, from simple observation to active involvement. Participating in these activities provides a unique experience not commonly available on other Maldivian islands while supporting the local farming community and helping preserve traditional agricultural knowledge."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'thakandhoo';


-- thimarafushi
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Thaa Atoll, Central Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island with Airport"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 2,500 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"2.1 km long, 1.3 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"215 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Domestic flight or seaplane"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Exceptional culture, amazing beaches, airport gateway"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, convenient access"}],"island_overview":["Thimarafushi Island is an exceptional local island in Thaa Atoll that offers visitors a vibrant glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. This remarkable island combines natural beauty with an energetic atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking exciting cultural experiences and amazing tropical surroundings.","Known for its gorgeous beaches, exceptional coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Thimarafushi provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s vibrant community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their dynamic way of life with exceptional hospitality.","What makes Thimarafushi special is its exceptional natural environment and vibrant island setting. Visitors can enjoy amazing beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience dynamic island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the exceptional Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Thimarafushi Island is strategically located in the central part of Thaa Atoll, approximately 215 kilometers from Male. This location provides an exceptional and vibrant experience while serving as the main gateway to Thaa Atoll through its domestic airport, making it highly accessible for travelers.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to amazing coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location and airport facilities make it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Thaa Atoll in its most exceptional form."]},{"heading":"Thimarafushi: Exceptional Paradise & Marine Excellence","paragraphs":["Thimarafushi Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring amazing white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most exceptional marine environments in Thaa Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a vibrant, dynamic setting."]},{"heading":"Amazing White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Thimarafushi features exceptional white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and dynamic beach activities."]},{"heading":"Exceptional House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers vibrant snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Vibrant Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the dynamic spirit of traditional island life with friendly locals and exceptional Maldivian culture in a vibrant community setting."]},{"heading":"Dynamic Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks and amazing islands around Thimarafushi for exceptional tropical paradise experiences with rich marine life."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Thimarafushi''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Thimarafushi feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Thimarafushi offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and exceptional activities. The island''s vibrant environment and dynamic atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in an amazing, energetic setting with convenient access to the entire atoll."]},{"heading":"Exceptional House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in exceptional waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby amazing dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in exceptional marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, amazing sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Thaa Atoll with vibrant exploration opportunities from the airport hub."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in exceptional community settings."]},{"heading":"Dynamic Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience exceptional Maldivian island life with vibrant cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy amazing sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in exceptional waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Thimarafushi is home to approximately 2,500 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism and modern connectivity through the island''s airport. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and exceptional cultural traditions that create a vibrant atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Thimarafushi follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities, enhanced by the island''s role as a transportation hub. The island maintains an exceptional atmosphere where visitors can experience vibrant Maldivian culture and customs in their most dynamic, energetic setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this exceptional island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Thimarafushi has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and exceptional cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Thimarafushi Island?","answer":"The island serves as the main gateway to Thaa Atoll with its domestic airport, making it easily accessible for travelers."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Thimarafushi?","answer":"The best time to visit Thimarafushi is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more exceptional local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Thimarafushi?","answer":"Thimarafushi offers various accommodations including exceptional guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a vibrant setting."},{"question":"What makes Thimarafushi''s accessibility special?","answer":"Thimarafushi is known for its exceptional accessibility as the main gateway to Thaa Atoll with its domestic airport. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a dynamic atmosphere perfect for energetic exploration with convenient connections to other islands in the atoll."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["guraidhoo","gaadhiffushi","dhiyamigili","burunee","vilufushi","veymandoo","vandhoo","omadhoo","madifushi","kinbidhoo","kandoodhoo","hirilandhoo"]}'::jsonb
