-- vaadhoo-gaafu-dhaalu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Vaadhoo Island?","answer":"There is no public ferry service to Vaadhoo, so private speedboat transfers must be arranged through your guesthouse or hotel."},{"question":"When is the best time to see the bioluminescence?","answer":"The bioluminescent plankton are present year-round but are most visible between June and December, especially during darker moon phases (new moon). The glow is typically most intense between 9pm and 2am on calm, dark nights with minimal light pollution."},{"question":"Is the bioluminescence guaranteed?","answer":"No, the bioluminescence is a natural phenomenon that can''t be guaranteed. Its intensity varies based on weather conditions, water temperature, plankton concentrations, and other environmental factors. However, Vaadhoo offers one of the most reliable locations to witness this phenomenon in the Maldives."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Vaadhoo?","answer":"As Vaadhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas (shoulders and knees covered). Swimwear is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach.\" When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Vaadhoo?","answer":"Vaadhoo''s waters offer excellent marine biodiversity, including healthy coral formations with both hard and soft corals. Common sightings include reef sharks, sea turtles, various ray species, and abundant reef fish. The atoll is particularly known for whale shark and manta ray sightings (seasonal)."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
